## Mutations after independent review

Only after the exact source, mutant, runner, restoration procedure, and expected assertion are independently CLEAR and a fresh slot grant exists. Mutate one predicate at a time from a byte-exact backup; do not edit profile/oracle fixtures. The following are mutation specifications, not authorization to execute. For each one, freeze the merged baseline source hash, make a unique run directory, copy the exact affected file byte-for-byte to `source-backup/`, record its SHA-256, apply only the stated one-predicate edit, record the mutant hash, and launch only the named test with `--exact --nocapture`. Immediately restore from that backup, touch the restored file and owned broker library source to prevent stale Cargo reuse, and verify the original SHA-256 before any next command. Preserve full original output/status and a separate correction record if metadata parsing is wrong; never edit the frozen attempt.

| ID | Exact mutation | Exact selected test | Expected failing assertion |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| N1 issuer admission | In `packages/aethyme/rust/crates/aethyme-broker/src/local_capture_notice.rs::ingest`, change `if revision.target != target_name || revision.issuer != issuer` to `if revision.target != target_name` (remove only issuer binding). | `local_capture_notice::tests::notice_ingress_refuses_unbound_issuer_revision_and_capture_without_admission_effects` | The existing `assert!(matches!(wrong_issuer, Err(NoticeError::Stale)))` fails because the wrong-issuer notice is accepted. |
| N2 old epoch tick | In `packages/aethyme/rust/crates/aethyme-broker/src/local_capture_notice.rs::consume_pending_locked`, remove only `|| body.authority_epoch != owner.authority_epoch().as_str()` from the stale predicate. | `local_capture_notice::tests::owner_tick_marks_notice_from_old_epoch_stale_without_admission_effects` | The exact detail assertion expects `Some("authority epoch or selected target revision changed")`; the old-epoch notice reaches the retained-capture mismatch path and reports a different reason. |
| S1 canonical appointment body | In `packages/aethyme/rust/crates/aethyme-broker/src/local_controller/service.rs::validate_status_binding`, remove only the `record.canonical_bytes() != body` refusal block. | `collaboration_cli::lifecycle::tests::service_status_rejects_corrupt_body_index_bindings_without_writes` | The `noncanonical_body` case's `service_status_for_store(...).unwrap_err()` panics because lookup accepts the noncanonical but parse-equivalent persisted body. |
| C1 exact receipt confirmation | In `packages/aethyme/rust/crates/aethyme-broker/src/collaboration_capture.rs::release_retention`, remove only `if confirmation != &receipt_record_id { return Err(CaptureError::ConfirmationMismatch { ... }) }`. | `collaboration_capture::tests::contribution_root_release_requires_exact_committed_receipt_and_is_idempotent` | The first wrong-confirmation assertion expecting `Err(CaptureError::ConfirmationMismatch { .. })` fails because release proceeds with the wrong receipt ID. |
| V1 unsupported inventory preflight | In `packages/aethyme/rust/crates/aethyme-broker/src/execution_verifier.rs::prepare`, remove only `ensure_supported_inventory(&inventory)?;`. | `execution_verifier::prepare_preflight_tests::prepare_rejects_nonzero_exit_before_runtime_or_capture_side_effects` | The assertion requiring `Err(VerificationError::Unsupported(detail))` with `detail == NONZERO_EXIT_UNSUPPORTED` fails; malformed commit processing returns a different error. |

For all five, require compile completion, the one named test selected and failed at the stated assertion, `0 passed; 1 failed`, status/exit 101, exact restored source hash, and unchanged runner/recorder/operator hashes. A compile failure, zero selected tests, another assertion, or a setup failure is preserved and uncredited. Exact route registration/help, history no-replay, CAP missing/uncommitted receipt, and native unknown-root tests remain positive regressions in the focused suite; do not claim they are mutation-qualified unless separately reviewed with a concrete mutant. No provider/model/held-out/replay work.

## Scope limits

The notice queue bounds pending rows at 512 project-wide, owner-tick batches at 512, and status response pages by the requested limit. Terminal notice/outcome audit history is append-only and has no automatic pruning or total-history cap; no total database-size bound is claimed. This plan does not claim T64 rehearsal completion, provider coverage, quality improvements, or reliability beyond the specifically observed finite commands.


